==Trivia==
*The name Idi may be derived from ''ID'', ''[[wikipedia:Id, ego and superego|id]]'', ''[[wikipedia:Eden|Eden]]'', 遺伝 ''iden'' (genetic heredity), アイディア ''aidia'' (idea), アイディアル ''aidiaru'' (ideal), or アイディリック ''aidirikku'' (idyllic).
*"Re" may stand for ''[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]'', ''ready'' (referring to her high movement speed and attack speed), ''repeat'' (as in "repeat of [[Idi:Ne]]", which would imply that Ne came before Re chronologically), ''retaliate'' (referring to how she can immediately strike again after a knockback), or レジェンド ''rejendo'' (legend).
*Her gender is confirmed by the description of the ''Elder Annihilator'' [[Meow Medals|Meow Medal]]: "Defeat Idi:Re and clear her stage."
*While Idi:Re's description states that she is Subject 002 (検体No.002, "Specimen No.002" in Japanese), the identity of Subject 001 is unknown. It may be:
**[[Relic Doge]], the only other [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] to appear in the [[Laboratory of Relics]].
**[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N001]], which would imply that Idi:Re hatched from the missing Ancient Egg: N002.
**[[Gigahaniwan]], as it is a Relic enhanced through genome editing in the Laboratory of Relics (though it does not appear there), while Idi:Re is also a Relic and may have been created synthetically.
*In Japanese, Idi:Re and Idi:Ne have very different descriptions from other enemies, using exclusively kanji and katakana, even for words that would normally be spelled using hiragana.
*She and Relic Doge are the only Relic enemies to appear in [[Stories of Legend]], both in the [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Eldritch Forces Invasion]].
*She has the second-highest attack power and money drop of any Relic enemy, only beaten by [[Zero Luza]]. She is also tied with [[Idi:Ne]] for the highest movement speed of all Relic enemies.
*Idi:Re, [[Ghost Doge]], [[Ghost Snache]], [[Ghost Baa Baa]] and [[Angel Fanboy]] are the only enemies in Stories of Legend that do not appear in Uncanny Legends.
**Idi:Re is the only one that was not introduced in an event stage.

